      "title": "Associate Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-23\n\nLocation: Rockville Centre\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter  Resume TYPE OF POSITION/EMPLOYMENT CATEGORY:   Full-Time DEPARTMENT: Admissions SCHEDULE: Monday-Friday, 9:00am to 5:00pm Occasional evening, holiday, weekend work required: Recruitment events happen nights, weekends and some holidays.  REMOTE WORK:  Available on occasion after 1 year of employment. TRAVEL: Occasional for recruitment events in the tri-state area, as well as regional and other conferences. HOURS/WEEK and MONTHS/YEAR:   35  hours/week and 52 weeks/year  FLSA STATUS: E xempt, Salaried  GENERAL PURPOSE The Associate Director of Admissions serves as a key leadership role within Molloy University’s Office of Admissions, with primary responsibility for undergraduate first-year and transfer student recruitment and enrollment communications strategy. This individual leads the design and execution of multi-channel, Slate-driven communication plans that leverage email, text, phone, print, and AI-assisted recruitment tools to engage prospective students at every stage of the enrollment funnel. The Associate Director serves as the team’s lead communications architect, supervising and mentoring admissions staff while fostering a collaborative, growth-oriented culture. This position requires a confident and creative enrollment professional who combines data-informed decision-making with a passion for building authentic relationships with students, families, and school counselors.  ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Enrollment Communications Strategy & Execution – Lead the design, development, and execution of Molloy’s multi-channel admissions communication plan using Slate CRM. This includes building and managing email campaigns, text message workflows, AI recruiter interactions, phone outreach, and print communications targeted at prospective students across all stages of the enrollment funnel. Serve as the office’s primary expert in Slate communication tools, ensuring communications are timely, personalized, and aligned with enrollment goals. Application Review & Admissions Counseling – Evaluate and process first-year undergraduate applications. Serve as a senior resource for application processing questions from admissions counselors and the operations team. Counsel prospective students and families through in-person appointments, phone calls, and email with a focus on yield conversion. Team Leadership, Training & Development – Supervise, mentor, and develop the admissions team, including counselors, assistant directors, and operations staff. Lead onboarding and implement a comprehensive training program that builds team capacity in Slate communications, AI recruiter tools, recruitment best practices, and customer service. Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, and professional growth. Undergraduate Recruitment & Travel – Attend and represent Molloy at undergraduate recruitment events, on-site evaluation days, high school visits, and college fairs during the fall and spring travel seasons. Conduct information sessions and build relationships with secondary school counselors. Travel is required. On-Campus Enrollment Events + Academic Liaison – Plan and execute high-quality on-campus recruitment events including Open Houses, Accepted Students Days, Counselor Breakfasts, and campus visit experiences. Provide oversight for the campus tour coordinator and ensure all events reflect Molloy’s brand and enrollment priorities. Serve as the direct liaison for at least one of Molloy’s academic schools, maintaining up-to-date knowledge of programs and communicating relevant updates to the team and prospective students. Uphold and continuously improve office policies and procedures, and troubleshoot Slate CRM and operational issues as they arise. REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree  Databases  5 to 8 years of experience in college admissions, enrollment management, or a closely related field.  Microsoft Office (Outlook, PowerPoint, Excel, Word)  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with Slate CRM and/or other admissions CRM platforms and Generative AI tools is strongly preferred.  Demonstrated experience developing and executing enrollment communications campaigns is highly desirable.  RESPONSIBILITY FOR PUBLIC CONTACT Daily contact requiring courtesy, discretion, and sound judgment. SALARY INFORMATION When determining the salary offer for a new employee, Molloy considers several key characteristics such as job knowledge, skills, and experience as well as internal and external equity. The hiring annual salary for this position is $68,000 to $71,000. This annual salary represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of compensation at the time of posting.   As part of its total compensation package, Molloy University offers an extensive range of benefits and programs for its employees including excellent health and dental insurance options, generous time off and tuition benefits. For further information, please visit  Benefits | Molloy University .  AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Women, minorities, persons with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply.  Molloy University does not discriminate on the basis of an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, or military status; in its administration of educational policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or in employment practices.   Molloy University takes its responsibility seriously to establish an environment in which the dignity and worth of all members of the institutional community are respected. In its effort to provide an optimal learning environment the University seeks the appointment of persons who are highly qualified and whose background is appropriate to fill each vacancy. It is University policy to recruit, employ, retain and promote employees without discrimination regarding sex, race, color, creed, religion, age, marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, national or ethnic origin or physical disability.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f1758074-bb0b-4d6b-8d46-3a90ce325365&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202998612981_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director of Financial Aid",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\n\nLocation: Rockville Centre\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter  Resume TYPE OF POSITION/EMPLOYMENT CATEGORY:   Full-Time DEPARTMENT: Financial Aid SCHEDULE: Monday-Friday, 9:00am to 5:00pm Occasional evening or weekend work required: Enrollment events - Open House, Accepted Students Day, etc.  REMOTE WORK: No HOURS/WEEK and MONTHS/YEAR:   35  hours/week and 52 weeks/year  FLSA STATUS: E xempt, Salaried  GENERAL PURPOSE The Director of Financial Aid serves as a key member of the Enrollment Management leadership team and is responsible for the strategic and operational leadership of the financial aid office. The Director is required to maintain a high-functioning, compliant, and efficient financial aid operation.  The ideal candidate will be an experienced, student-first professional prepared to modernize our aid programs, leverage cutting-edge tools, and build a best-in-class financial aid operation that directly supports enrollment growth, student retention, and institutional sustainability.  ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Oversee all core aid processes: FAFSA processing, verification, packaging, disbursement, SAP reviews, R2T4 calculations, and student counseling and appeals. This includes managing required federal and state reporting (FISAP, IPEDS, Common Data Set, TAP/NYS aid reconciliations) and coordinating audits with Finance and external auditors.  Serve as the institution's primary Title IV compliance officer; ensure adherence to all federal, New York State, and institutional regulations governing financial aid. Stay current with evolving federal and NY State aid regulations and proactively implement required changes; bringing a solutions-oriented mindset to complex regulatory challenges.  Partner with the VP for Enrollment Management and AVP for Admissions & Enrollment Technology, Marketing, Athletics, and Academic Affairs to develop and execute aid strategies that drive recruitment, yield, and retention. This requires designing and refining merit- and need-based packaging models that are competitive, equitable, and informed by market data and enrollment analytics. Lead with and develop an office culture focusing on championing a student-first philosophy; ensuring that every interaction with the financial aid office is accessible, transparent, and empowering for students and families. The Director will lead, mentor, and develop a dedicated financial aid team; fostering a culture of collaboration, accountability, and continuous improvement. The Director will set clear performance expectations and provide ongoing coaching, training, and professional development for the team.  Oversee all interfaces with Department of Education systems (COD, NSLDS, FAA Access) and NY State systems ensuring accurate and timely data integrity across all platforms and systems. REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree  Minimum of 5-7 years of progressive financial aid experience, including at least 2 years in a leadership role (Assistant Director, Associate Director, or Director) Demonstrated  knowledge of federal Title IV regulations, NY State aid programs (TAP, HESC), and compliance best practices.  Experience with PowerFAIDS, Jenzabar, or comparable financial aid management and SIS platforms.  Strong analytical skills with the ability to translate data into actionable enrollment and aid strategy. Excellent communication skills, including the ability to present complex financial aid information clearly to diverse audiences. Proven ability to lead and develop teams in a fast-paced, student-focused environment. Student-first mindset with a commitment to access, equity, and outstanding service. Microsoft Office (Outlook, PowerPoint, Excel, Word)  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Higher Education Administration, Business, or a related field. 7+ years of financial aid experience, including leadership at a private, non-profit institution. Experience with Slate CRM and financial aid leveraging tools (e.g., RNL). Familiarity with NY State financial aid programs and HESC reporting. Track record of modernizing financial aid operations and implementing process improvements. Experience working in enrollment management as part of a collaborative, data-driven leadership team.  Experience with NCAA Div. II Athletics and aid regulations. RESPONSIBILITY FOR PUBLIC CONTACT Daily contact requiring courtesy, discretion, and sound judgment. SALARY INFORMATION When determining the salary offer for a new employee, Molloy considers several key characteristics such as job knowledge, skills, and experience as well as internal and external equity. The hiring annual salary for this position is $120,000 to $135,000. This annual salary represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of compensation at the time of posting.   As part of its total compensation package, Molloy University offers an extensive range of benefits and programs for its employees including excellent health and dental insurance options, generous time off and tuition benefits. For further information, please visit  Benefits | Molloy University .  AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Women, minorities, persons with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply.  Molloy University does not discriminate on the basis of an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, or military status; in its administration of educational policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or in employment practices.   Molloy University takes its responsibility seriously to establish an environment in which the dignity and worth of all members of the institutional community are respected. In its effort to provide an optimal learning environment the University seeks the appointment of persons who are highly qualified and whose background is appropriate to fill each vacancy. It is University policy to recruit, employ, retain and promote employees without discrimination regarding sex, race, color, creed, religion, age, marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, national or ethnic origin or physical disability.",
      "department": ""
    },
