      "title": "Per Diem Nursing Lab Instructor",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-12-04\n\nLocation: Rockville Centre\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter  Resume TYPE OF POSITION/EMPLOYMENT CATEGORY:   Seasonal  DEPARTMENT: Clinical Learning Center SCHEDULE: Monday - Friday,   Hours may vary between 7:30am to 6:00pm.  Occasional evenings and weekends may be required for department and university needs. REMOTE WORK Eligible: No FLSA STATUS: Non-E xempt, Hourly GENERAL PURPOSE Assist undergraduate and graduate nursing students with practice and competency evaluation of nursing skills in a supportive, nurturing, clinical environment. Participates in Simulation Based Education (SBE) across nursing curriculums. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES   Provide nursing students with the support necessary to practice nursing skills. Administer competency evaluation of psychomotor skills for undergraduate students with reinforcement and remediation of nursing skills as warranted.  Facilitate simulation experiences: setup, scenario competency, breakdown of environment, and debriefing. Assist with the day-to-day activities of the CLC. Assist with maintenance of laboratory environment, inventory of supplies and equipment. REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree (Registered Nurse, B.S.N) 5 to 8 years of clinical/simulation experience  Microsoft Office (Outlook, Excel, Word)  RESPONSIBILITY FOR PUBLIC CONTACT Daily contact requiring courtesy, discretion, and sound judgment. SALARY INFORMATION When determining the salary offer for a new employee, Molloy considers several key characteristics such as job knowledge, skills, and experience as well as internal and external equity. The hiring hourly rate for this position is $40.00. This hourly pay rate represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of compensation at the time of posting.   As part of its total compensation package, Molloy University offers an extensive range of benefits and programs for its employees including generous time off and tuition benefits. For further information, please visit  Benefits | Molloy University .  AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Women, minorities, persons with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply.  Molloy University does not discriminate on the basis of an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, or military status; in its administration of educational policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or in employment practices.   Molloy University takes its responsibility seriously to establish an environment in which the dignity and worth of all members of the institutional community are respected. In its effort to provide an optimal learning environment the University seeks the appointment of persons who are highly qualified and whose background is appropriate to fill each vacancy. It is University policy to recruit, employ, retain and promote employees without discrimination regarding sex, race, color, creed, religion, age, marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, national or ethnic origin or physical disability.",
